t landed."], "observations": ["The finish quality of the renders (flat shading, clean silhouettes) is roughly at the level of the spruce anchor (anchor-0). The anchor was used for finish quality only.", "In render-2 (P-TRUNK, seed 1), seen from a lower and closer angle, the fronds look longer and more recurved, and the lower fronds hang below the crown base. They still read as short and thin compared with reference-1.", "The render-3 metadata marks visibility as 'hidden', yet the image clearly shows a close-up of the trunk surface. I judged what is drawn and noted the conflict.", "reference-2 is labelled P-BASE but shows the mid-trunk, not the ground-level base. It is still valid evidence for the leaf-base pattern at close range.", "In render-0 (seed 1), the trunk is straight with a moderate taper and a small flare at the base. That is within 'near-constant' at catalogue level.", "Both whole-tree renders show a single unbranched stem. Nothing grows on either trunk; the only things on it are small stubs, which are leaf-base proxies, not growth.", "Relative progress (the trunk organs from fn-110 are present as stubs) does not mean the render is ready in absolute terms."], "findings": [{"observation": "The crown in both seeds reads as a palm-like radial rosette of pinnate fronds. The fronds are short and mostly straight, and in the whole-tree views the lowest ones droop only slightly. The references show long, strongly arching fronds and a large crown relative to the trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet size may be too low, and frond droop or curvature too weak. The owner already names leaflet size and frond length as the first dials."}, {"observation": "The leaflets are short and small instead of long, narrow and stiff, so the fronds look thin rather than bristly and plumose.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The leaflet length or size dial may be too low."}, {"observation": "The trunk surface is smooth, with a few scattered conical stubs. There is no spiral diamond lattice and no fibrous matting.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The stubs from fn-110 may be too sparse or too small. A fibre layer may not be expressed by the generator."}, {"observation": "The seed 42 trunk bends noticeably just below the crown after a lean the other way lower down, so it is not straight or gently leaning.", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The trunk's curvature or gravitropism variance may be too high for some seeds."}, {"observation": "The seed 1 trunk is straight, with a moderate taper and a basal flare.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk in either seed. The reference epiphytes are scene features (variation), and the owner does not want them.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "There are no fruit clusters. The core inventory trait is not expressed, and the owner config lists fn-111 as not landed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The generator does not yet have a fruit-cluster organ."}, {"observation": "There is no dead-frond skirt. This is a secondary trait and optional refinement.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status"